course: dictionary
lesson: 10288
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tortoiseshell is one word with more than one meaning. It can be a shell, a pattern, a cat or a butterfly. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it. They are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «almost all tortoiseshell and calico cats are female» Here the word «cats» comes right after tortoiseshell, so a tortoiseshell must be a cat. Check it by swapping in your meaning: a tortoiseshell cat is still a cat, so the swap makes sense.
explain: Tortoiseshell can also be an adjective, a word that describes a thing. In «tortoiseshell glasses», the word means a brown and amber pattern like the shell, not a real shell. Glasses cannot be made from a cat, so the clue is in the word glasses.
fact: Tortoiseshell is the hard, brown and yellow shell of the hawksbill sea turtle, not of tortoises.
fact: Trading hawksbill tortoiseshell is now banned to protect the turtles.
fact: A tortoiseshell cat has a coat with black and orange patches, and almost all of them are female.
fact: The small tortoiseshell is a common British garden butterfly with orange, black and yellow wings.
fact: Tortoiseshell can also mean a brown and amber pattern copied in plastic, as in tortoiseshell glasses.
exercise: The small tortoiseshell landed on the buddleia in the garden. What is a tortoiseshell here? | *A butterfly with orange, black and yellow wings | A hard shell from a sea turtle | A kind of comb | A pair of glasses
exercise: Mia's cat has black and orange patches, and her family calls it a tortoiseshell. What is a tortoiseshell here? | *A cat with a black and orange coat | A kind of bird | A small turtle from the sea | A shell from a tortoise's back
exercise: Why is trading hawksbill tortoiseshell banned? | To make glasses cheaper | *To protect the turtles | Because it is too soft to use | Because tortoises are too fast
test: Which word after tortoiseshell helps you know it is a cat in «almost all tortoiseshell and calico cats are female»? | almost | are | *cats | all
test: In «tortoiseshell glasses», what does tortoiseshell describe? | A cat with patches | A small garden butterfly | *A brown and amber pattern like the shell | A hard turtle shell
exam: Why does the word tortoiseshell not always mean something from a tortoise? | *Because the shell comes from hawksbill sea turtles | Because tortoises have no shells | Because it only means a cat | Because tortoises are rare
